WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.377
Domain 3 primer: Claude Code Configuration & Workflows.

2
00:00:04.377 --> 00:00:12.553
Domain 3 is about setting up Claude Code so a whole team gets consistent, well-scoped help, in the editor and in CI.

3
00:00:13.953 --> 00:00:19.816
Claude Code is an agent that reads your files, runs commands and edits code from your terminal.

4
00:00:19.816 --> 00:00:25.000
Domain three is about configuring it well and choosing good ways of working with it.

5
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:32.961
It is about a fifth of the exam and shows up in the code generation, developer productivity and continuous integration scenarios.

6
00:00:34.361 --> 00:00:36.239
Five terms carry this domain.

7
00:00:36.239 --> 00:00:39.930
CLAUDE dot md holds instructions loaded in every session.

8
00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:44.397
The rules folder holds topic files that can be tied to file patterns.

9
00:00:44.397 --> 00:00:48.282
Commands and skills are saved workflows you run when needed.

10
00:00:48.282 --> 00:00:51.261
Plan mode makes Claude propose before editing.

11
00:00:51.261 --> 00:00:56.505
And the print flag runs Claude once, without a person, for scripts and pipelines.

12
00:00:57.905 --> 00:01:01.213
Most domain three questions reduce to two questions.

13
00:01:01.213 --> 00:01:06.682
When does this instruction load: always, only for matching files, or only when called?

14
00:01:06.682 --> 00:01:13.615
And who receives it: everyone who clones the repository, or only the person whose home folder holds the file?

15
00:01:13.615 --> 00:01:18.257
Answer those two and most configuration questions become straightforward.

16
00:01:19.657 --> 00:01:21.973
The task statements build on each other.

17
00:01:21.973 --> 00:01:25.851
Three point one and three point three are about standing knowledge.

18
00:01:25.851 --> 00:01:28.456
Three point two is about on demand workflows.

19
00:01:28.456 --> 00:01:34.245
Three point four and three point five are about your working style: when to plan and how to iterate.

20
00:01:34.245 --> 00:01:39.860
Three point six takes everything into continuous integration, where Claude runs without a person.

21
00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:43.565
Here are the words this domain uses most.

22
00:01:43.565 --> 00:01:46.657
Pause the video and read through them, then keep going.

23
00:01:48.057 --> 00:01:53.727
Carry two questions into every domain three item: when does this load, and who gets it?

24
00:01:53.727 --> 00:01:58.355
Keep team standards in the repository and personal preferences at home.

25
00:01:58.355 --> 00:02:02.265
Plan big, uncertain changes and execute small ones directly.

26
00:02:02.265 --> 00:02:05.785
And in pipelines, run headless with structured output.

27
00:02:05.785 --> 00:02:08.196
The lessons ahead fill in each piece.

